### Test confirms webServer runs before globalSetup

Source: https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/main/tests/playwright-test/web-server.spec.ts

Tests with both webServer array and globalSetup prove the order: globalSetup imports fetch and makes HTTP requests to the server started by webServer, confirming the server is already running.

```typescript
    'playwright.config.ts': `
        module.exports = {
          webServer: [
            {
              command: 'node ${JSON.stringify(SIMPLE_SERVER_PATH)} ${port}',
              url: 'http://localhost:${port}/port',
            },
            {
              command: 'node ${JSON.stringify(SIMPLE_SERVER_PATH)} ${port + 1}',
              url: 'http://localhost:${port + 1}/port',
            }
          ],
          globalSetup: 'globalSetup.ts',
          globalTeardown: 'globalTeardown.ts',
        };
        `,
    'globalSetup.ts': `
